 approval. Copied: low-level-requirements.toml (re-attested: LLR-278); test-cases.toml (re-attested: TC-278). Registries not named by this act keep their prior snapshot bytes."," - 2026-10-18 — refresh under approval. Copied: low-level-requirements.toml (re-attested: LLR-300, LLR-322); test-cases.toml (re-attested: TC-345). Registries not named by this act keep their prior snapshot bytes."," - 2026-10-18 — refresh under approval. Copied: low-level-requirements.toml (re-attested: LLR-278, LLR-310, LLR-338); test-cases.toml (re-attested: TC-278). Registries not named by this act keep their prior snapshot bytes.","+- 2026-10-18 — refresh under approval. Copied: system-requirements.toml (re-attested: SR-209); low-level-requirements.toml (re-attested: LLR-248). Registries not named by this act keep their prior snapshot bytes."]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-918\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\acts.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":798,"oldLines":3,"newStart":798,"newLines":9,"lines":[" date = \"2026-10-18\""," approved = []"," reattested = [\"LLR-278\", \"LLR-310\", \"LLR-338\", \"TC-278\"]","+","+[[act]]","+seq = 132","+date = \"2026-10-18\"","+approved = []","+reattested = [\"LLR-248\", \"SR-209\"]"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-918\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\low-level-requirements.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":2606,"oldLines":8,"newStart":2606,"newLines":8,"lines":[" sr_refs = [\"SR-209\"]"," title = \"Every loop writer carries the trailer, and the floor checks it\""," module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/integrate.py;project-trajectory/scripts/intake.py;project-trajectory/scripts/handback.py;project-trajectory/scripts/agent_common.py;project-trajectory/hooks/commit-msg;project-trajectory/scripts/bookkeeping.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/provenance.py\"","-code_symbol = \"_claim_locked/_mint/commit_telemetry/_loop_trailer_refusal/_commit_object/LOOP_WRITER_SUBJECTS/loop_writer_commit/loop_lane_window\"","-detail = \"The claim, refresh, merge, bookkeeping, handback-close and telemetry writers append format_loop_trailer to their messages; the claim and the mint do so through bookkeeping._commit_object, the commit helper both share. The commit-msg hook runs loop_trailer_refusal when the loop marker is set. integrate._loop_trailer_refusal, in the merge ladder, re-checks the commits of every loop lane whoever runs the slot, since plumbing commits and --no-verify commits never reach the hook and hooks are opt-in per checkout. A lane is the loop's when its claim, or any commit one of the loop's own writers made in its range, carries the trailer (kitlib.provenance.loop_writer_commit: a well-formed trailer and a subject a loop writer composes). Every commit of a loop lane must carry a present, well-formed trailer, a person's commit included, which otherwise belongs in the person's own lane; the commits before the lane's first marked loop-writer commit are exempt from this rung only (kitlib.provenance.loop_lane_window). commit_telemetry reports a refused telemetry commit instead of swallowing it.\"","+code_symbol = \"_claim_locked/_mint/commit_telemetry/_loop_trailer_refusal/_commit_object/LOOP_WRITER_SUBJECTS/loop_writer_commit/loop_lane_window/reclaim_subject/_reclaim\"","+detail = \"The claim, refresh, merge, bookkeeping, handback-close and telemetry writers append format_loop_trailer to their messages; the claim and the mint do so through bookkeeping._commit_object, the commit helper both share. The commit-msg hook runs loop_trailer_refusal when the loop marker is set. integrate._loop_trailer_refusal, in the merge ladder, re-checks the commits of every loop lane whoever runs the slot, since plumbing commits and --no-verify commits never reach the hook and hooks are opt-in per checkout. A lane is the loop's when its claim, or any commit one of the loop's own writers made in its range, carries the trailer (kitlib.provenance.loop_writer_commit: a well-formed trailer and a subject a loop writer composes). Every commit of a loop lane must carry a present, well-formed trailer, a person's commit included, which otherwise belongs in the person's own lane; the commits before the lane's first marked loop-writer commit are exempt from this rung only (kitlib.provenance.loop_lane_window). Lane commits are read oldest first, each with its parents and tree, and each parent outside the range is read for its tree. The window opens at a loop claim or a marked loop-writer commit and closes at an attended re-claim with exactly one parent, a tree equal to that parent's, this branch's re-claim subject exactly, and no provenance trailer at all. A re-claim met while the window is closed changes nothing. The commits after a re-claim are exempt from this rung until the next marked loop-writer commit re-opens the window; a lane never marked has no window. The re-claim subject has one composer, which the coordinator's procedure and the reader use. commit_telemetry reports a refused telemetry commit instead of swallowing it.\""," status = \"Approved\""," component = \"CMP-008\""," phase = 6"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-918\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\system-requirements.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":1458,"oldLines":7,"newStart":1458,"newLines":7,"lines":[" hat_refs = [\"SECURITY\", \"UNATTENDED-OPS\"]"," requirement = \"When a commit is made from a process the unattended loop started, or is merged in a lane the loop owns from the point the loop took that lane over, the delivered commit floor shall refuse it unless it carries a valid provenance trailer naming the loop and its session.\""," rationale = \"\"\"A status change on a human-held rung can be told apart from a human's only if every loop-made commit says it is one. Without a floor that holds every loop commit to it, a trailer could appear on only some of the loop's commits and a missing one would prove nothing. Where a commit is made, the condition is who made it, not when: a person committing in another checkout while the loop runs is not the loop. Where a lane merges, the floor sees commits, not processes, so it reads whose lane it is from the commits and judges every commit of a loop lane, a person's included: there an unmarked commit the loop made cannot be told from a person's, and a person's commit belongs in the person's own lane. The commits made before the loop took a lane over are exempt, since nothing then could have marked them. Refusing the unmarked commit at the floor makes the mark total, which is what lets a later check treat its absence as meaningful. The floor where a commit is made is local and a determined bypass defeats it, which is why the merge re-checks a loop lane and the history check stands behind both.\"\"\"","-acceptance_criteria = \"Every process the loop starts carries a marker the commit floor reads, so a commit made from a loop-started process is known as the loop's; such a commit with no trailer, or with a malformed one, is refused naming the commit's subject; a commit made by a process the loop did not start needs no trailer and passes where it is made, even while the loop is running; the same validity rule, a trailer that is present and well-formed, applies wherever the commit floor runs. Where the floor judges a lane's commits at its merge, it reads whose lane it is from the commits: a lane is the loop's when its claim, or any commit one of the loop's own writers made in its range, carries the trailer. Every commit of a loop lane is then judged, whoever runs the merge, so a person's commit there must carry the trailer or move to the person's own lane; the commits before the lane's first trailer-carrying loop-writer commit are exempt from this check; a lane that is not the loop's is not judged.\"","+acceptance_criteria = \"Every process the loop starts carries a marker the commit floor reads, so a commit made from a loop-started process is known as the loop's; such a commit with no trailer, or with a malformed one, is refused naming the commit's subject; a commit made by a process the loop did not start needs no trailer and passes where it is made, even while the loop is running; the same validity rule, a trailer that is present and well-formed, applies wherever the commit floor runs. Where the floor judges a lane's commits at its merge, it reads whose lane it is from the commits: a lane is the loop's when its claim, or any commit one of the loop's own writers made in its range, carries the trailer. Every commit of a loop lane is then judged, whoever runs the merge, so a person's commit there must carry the trailer or move to the person's own lane; the commits before the lane's first trailer-carrying loop-writer commit are exempt from this check; a lane that is not the loop's is not judged. An attended re-claim recorded in the lane, a commit that changes nothing against its one parent, names that lane in the re-claim form, and carries no provenance trailer at all, ends the loop's window for the commits after it; a commit that fails any of those conditions is judged like any other; a later loop-writer commit re-opens the window.\""," priority = \"M\""," verification = \"Test\""," status = \"Approved\""]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-918\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\README.md","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-918\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\acts.toml","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-918\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\low-level-requirements.toml","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-918\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\system-requirements.toml"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FC9LLXnjsDAu9VgVS6WfpM","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
